{
  "definition": "What a call site of bench/fixtures/java/shop-java is, written from what Java does (JLS 15.12), not from what ripple prints, and checked against javac's own invoke instructions (tests/test_java_ground_truth.py compiles the fixture when a JDK is there). A site is a file, a line, the text written there and the symbol it is in. `call` is the name of the callee symbol it is about (the method's name, or `<init>` for a constructor, or the class's name for a class that is its own constructor), because a line can hold several calls. `edges` is EXACTLY the set of `kind callee` ripple must record for that call at that site: a proven call is an edge, and a dispatch to the methods that override it is an `override` edge. `unresolved` is a fragment the reason of the one unresolved call of that name at that site must contain: the call is not proven, and ripple says why. `never` are edges that must not exist, each a wrong answer the rules were written to avoid, with the line it would be written at. `layout` is what the walk and the declarations must say about files.",
  "fixture": "shop-java",
  "sites": [
    {"id": "overload-arity-and-super-trap", "group": "overloads", "file": "src/main/java/com/acme/shop/BulkCart.java", "line": 24, "text": "add(\"bulk\")", "caller": "com.acme.shop.BulkCart.fill()", "call": "add", "edges": ["call com.acme.shop.Cart.add(String)"], "why": "BulkCart declares add(Item,int), Cart declares add(String): a call with one String is Cart's, found through the superclass. The first class that has the NAME would be wrong."},
    {"id": "overload-in-subclass", "group": "overloads", "file": "src/main/java/com/acme/shop/BulkCart.java", "line": 25, "text": "add(Item.free(\"x\"), 2)", "caller": "com.acme.shop.BulkCart.fill()", "call": "add", "edges": ["call com.acme.shop.BulkCart.add(Item,int)"], "why": "two arguments: the subclass's own overload, the only one of that arity"},
    {"id": "overload-by-return-type", "group": "overloads", "file": "src/main/java/com/acme/shop/BulkCart.java", "line": 26, "text": "this.add(Item.free(\"y\"))", "caller": "com.acme.shop.BulkCart.fill()", "call": "add", "edges": ["call com.acme.shop.Cart.add(Item)"], "why": "two overloads take one argument; the argument is Item.free(...), whose declared return type is Item, exactly one overload's parameter"},
    {"id": "static-factory", "group": "overloads", "file": "src/main/java/com/acme/shop/BulkCart.java", "line": 25, "text": "add(Item.free(\"x\"), 2)", "caller": "com.acme.shop.BulkCart.fill()", "call": "free", "edges": ["call com.acme.shop.Item.free(String)"], "why": "a static method of a record, called through the type name"},
    {"id": "super-call-by-exact-type", "group": "overloads", "file": "src/main/java/com/acme/shop/BulkCart.java", "line": 14, "text": "super.add(item)", "caller": "com.acme.shop.BulkCart.add(Item,int)", "call": "add", "edges": ["call com.acme.shop.Cart.add(Item)"], "why": "super.m() is exact: it is the superclass's declaration and no override is a candidate"},
    {"id": "overload-delegates-by-return-type", "group": "overloads", "file": "src/main/java/com/acme/shop/Cart.java", "line": 29, "text": "add(Item.free(name))", "caller": "com.acme.shop.Cart.add(String)", "call": "add", "edges": ["call com.acme.shop.Cart.add(Item)"], "why": "the declared return type of Item.free picks add(Item) among the two one-argument overloads"},
    {"id": "overload-by-new", "group": "overloads", "file": "src/main/java/com/acme/shop/Cart.java", "line": 33, "text": "add(new Item(name, cents))", "caller": "com.acme.shop.Cart.add(String,int)", "call": "add", "edges": ["call com.acme.shop.Cart.add(Item)"], "why": "new Item(...) has the type Item"},
    {"id": "overload-by-arity", "group": "overloads", "file": "src/test/java/com/acme/shop/CartTest.java", "line": 7, "text": "c.add(\"a\", 250)", "caller": "com.acme.shop.CartTest.addsItems()", "call": "add", "edges": ["call com.acme.shop.Cart.add(String,int)"], "why": "only one overload takes two arguments"},
    {"id": "overload-by-new-argument", "group": "overloads", "file": "src/test/java/com/acme/shop/CartTest.java", "line": 8, "text": "c.add(new Item(\"b\", 100))", "caller": "com.acme.shop.CartTest.addsItems()", "call": "add", "edges": ["call com.acme.shop.Cart.add(Item)"], "why": "new Item(...) has the type Item"},
    {"id": "overload-by-var", "group": "overloads", "file": "src/main/java/com/acme/shop/Chains.java", "line": 18, "text": "c.add(\"v\")", "caller": "com.acme.shop.Chains.typed()", "call": "add", "edges": ["call com.acme.shop.Cart.add(String)"], "why": "c is a `var` initialised with new Cart(), so a Cart; a string literal is a String"},
    {"id": "overload-by-typed-local", "group": "overloads", "file": "src/main/java/com/acme/shop/Chains.java", "line": 20, "text": "c.add(item)", "caller": "com.acme.shop.Chains.typed()", "call": "add", "edges": ["call com.acme.shop.Cart.add(Item)"], "why": "item is declared Item"},
    {"id": "overload-string-concatenation", "group": "overloads", "file": "src/main/java/com/acme/shop/Cart.java", "line": 24, "text": "log.info(\"added \" + item.name())", "caller": "com.acme.shop.Cart.add(Item)", "call": "info", "edges": ["call com.acme.util.Log.info(String)"], "why": "a string literal plus anything is a String, the exact parameter of info(String); javac takes it over the varargs overload (JLS 15.12.2, phase 1)"},
    {"id": "overload-varargs-only-applicable", "group": "overloads", "file": "src/main/java/com/acme/shop/Cart.java", "line": 25, "text": "log.info(\"added %s\", item)", "caller": "com.acme.shop.Cart.add(Item)", "call": "info", "edges": ["call com.acme.util.Log.info(String,Object...)"], "why": "two arguments: only the varargs overload takes that many"},
    {"id": "overload-arguments-not-known", "group": "overloads", "file": "src/main/java/com/acme/shop/Cart.java", "line": 81, "text": "log.info(item.name())", "caller": "com.acme.shop.Cart.show(Item)", "call": "info", "edges": [], "unresolved": "2 overloads of info", "why": "item.name() is a record accessor, a call ripple does not give a type: the argument's type is not known, so no overload is picked"},
    {"id": "overload-arguments-not-known-2", "group": "overloads", "file": "src/main/java/com/acme/util/Log.java", "line": 18, "text": "info(String.format(fmt, args))", "caller": "com.acme.util.Log.info(String,Object...)", "call": "info", "edges": [], "unresolved": "2 overloads of info", "why": "String.format is a JDK call: its return type is not known"},
    {"id": "overload-by-cast", "group": "overloads", "file": "src/main/java/com/acme/util/Money.java", "line": 11, "text": "format((int) cents)", "caller": "com.acme.util.Money.format(long)", "call": "format", "edges": ["call com.acme.util.Money.format(int)"], "why": "a cast is the type it names: int"},
    {"id": "overload-widening-is-not-used", "group": "overloads", "file": "src/main/java/com/acme/util/Money.java", "line": 19, "text": "format(cents)", "caller": "com.acme.util.Money.of(short)", "call": "format", "edges": [], "unresolved": "2 overloads of format", "why": "javac widens the short to int, but widening is never used to pick: unresolved, not guessed"},
    {"id": "overload-by-declared-return", "group": "overloads", "file": "src/main/java/com/acme/shop/Cart.java", "line": 53, "text": "format(total())", "caller": "com.acme.shop.Cart.receipt()", "call": "format", "edges": ["call com.acme.util.Money.format(int)"], "why": "a single static import of Money.format; total() is declared int, exactly format(int)"},

    {"id": "strict-external-supertype-1", "group": "strict", "file": "src/main/java/com/acme/shop/Ledger.java", "line": 26, "text": "write(item)", "caller": "com.acme.shop.Ledger.record(Item)", "call": "write", "edges": [], "unresolved": "may declare another write", "why": "Ledger extends java.io.Writer, which ripple knows nothing about: a call of write may be one of Writer's"},
